# Build contexts for infra/docker/*.Dockerfile start at the REPOSITORY ROOT — a pnpm workspace
# cannot be installed from a subdirectory — so without this every build uploads node_modules,
# build output and .git to the daemon. Measured on a clean clone: ~4.5 GB down to ~30 MB.
#
# `infra/fakes` builds with its own context (`infra/fakes`), so this file does not apply to it.

# pnpm install and pnpm deploy both read the store, never the checked-out tree.
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Produced by the build stage inside the image; shipping the host's copy would make the image
# depend on a dirty local tree and would silently mask a broken build.
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/.turbo
**/.tanstack
**/.astro
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# .git is ~100 MB and no layer here needs a single commit.
.git

# Secret. `.env.example` IS copied — it is committed, it is the template, and a reviewer reading
# the Dockerfile should be able to see which variables the image expects.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Nothing in an image build touches these, and they are the largest directories in the tree.
shots
.cache
.tmp
.expo-cache
.kilo
openapi-out.log
prompt.txt